# Internal strategy / competitive / assessment docs — never commit.
#
# docs/internal/ was the intended home for this material, but most of it never
# landed there: 31 files sat tracked at the repo root, in docs/, and under
# control-plane/docs/CMA/ — PRFAQs, launch materials, the OSPO justification,
# comparative market analysis, positioning, funding plans, and the investment
# business case. This repo is private today, so that was invisible; it stops
# being invisible the moment the repo goes public, and that door only opens one
# way. Hence patterns by *name* as well as by directory.
#
# Note that .gitignore does nothing for files git already tracks. If one of
# these reappears in `git status` as staged, it was added with `git add -f` or
# predates these rules — untrack it with `git rm --cached`, don't just re-ignore.
docs/internal/

# Product/market strategy by name, wherever it lands
PRFAQ*
launch-materials*
*Launch Materials*
*Launch-Materials*
OSPO*Business*Justification*
control-plane/docs/CMA/
control-plane/docs/CMA.docx
*Investment Business Case*
*Funding Plan*
*funding_support*
*unconventional_paths*
*cio_questions*
*Features Worth Building*
# Competitor comparisons. Scoped to documents, not a bare *-vs-* — that would
# also swallow any source file that happens to use the word.
*-vs-*.docx
*-vs-*.pdf
*-vs-*.md

# Draft snapshots written by Office/Pages alongside the originals
.versions/
